WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.411 --> 00:00:02.244
- [Narrator] What if I told you

00:00:02.244 --> 00:00:03.435
some of the best Indian food in LA

00:00:03.435 --> 00:00:05.303
is next to this busy highway

00:00:05.303 --> 00:00:06.353
at a gas station

00:00:06.353 --> 00:00:07.822
inside a convenience store.

00:00:07.822 --> 00:00:09.478
This guy certainly likes it.
- Mmm-mm!

00:00:09.478 --> 00:00:11.117
- [Narrator] Let's see how
this plate of Indian burritos

00:00:11.117 --> 00:00:13.700
ended up near the Dorito aisle.

00:00:16.714 --> 00:00:18.091
At The Bombay Frankie Company,

00:00:18.091 --> 00:00:19.281
you'll find Hiram and his staff

00:00:19.281 --> 00:00:21.550
making Indian food at a gas station.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:22.614
Hiram, care to explain?

00:00:22.614 --> 00:00:25.431
- Okay, the reason why we chose
this particular gas station

00:00:25.431 --> 00:00:26.329
is because our family

00:00:26.329 --> 00:00:28.805
is actually in the gas station
convenience store business.

00:00:28.805 --> 00:00:30.915
We had this space free for quite a while

00:00:30.915 --> 00:00:32.976
and we thought well,
what a great launch pad.

00:00:32.976 --> 00:00:35.504
Traditionally what you
might find is unhealthy,

00:00:35.504 --> 00:00:36.754
non-fresh fare,

00:00:38.313 --> 00:00:39.526
and when you're coming across something

00:00:39.526 --> 00:00:41.471
that's not only fresh

00:00:41.471 --> 00:00:44.155
but is true to the most raw ingredients.

00:00:44.155 --> 00:00:47.033
So when we start with that
completely off-the-wall pairing

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.753
you're gonna be starting
from a really low point,

00:00:48.753 --> 00:00:51.719
so all you can go is high and higher.

00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:56.024
And we're trying to just
set the bar really high.

00:00:56.024 --> 00:00:57.887
- [Narrator] Since they've
opened, The Bombay Frankie Company

00:00:57.887 --> 00:01:00.795
has received both critical
and commercial success.

00:01:00.795 --> 00:01:03.770
- Definitely our most
popular item is the Frankie.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:06.372
In Bombay, sometimes it can
be a rolled up sandwich,

00:01:06.372 --> 00:01:08.834
sometimes it can be an enclosed sandwich.

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:11.018
What we try to do is make
it ultimately relatable

00:01:11.018 --> 00:01:14.734
to the LA market and make it
really similar to a burrito.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:16.723
It's one of the best
things you've ever tried.

00:01:16.723 --> 00:01:19.525
People say never mix business
with friends or family.

00:01:19.525 --> 00:01:21.683
I say don't knock it until you try it.

00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:23.753
The key members of The
Bombay Frankie Company

00:01:23.753 --> 00:01:26.428
is my sister, Priyanka,
- Please hold.

00:01:26.428 --> 00:01:29.023
- Our esteemed chef, Mr. Kamaljit Singh,

00:01:29.023 --> 00:01:30.190
and our staff.

00:01:34.099 --> 00:01:36.119
Having someone come in for the first time

00:01:36.119 --> 00:01:37.658
who's never tried Indian food

00:01:37.658 --> 00:01:40.326
and are completely
engulfed by the experience,

00:01:40.326 --> 00:01:44.156
they truly realize that
not only is it Indian food

00:01:44.156 --> 00:01:46.732
coming from a gas station and
being served in a gas station,

00:01:46.732 --> 00:01:48.619
that they would try it elsewhere.

00:01:48.619 --> 00:01:50.389
So by preserving traditional ingredients,

00:01:50.389 --> 00:01:53.023
traditional preparations,
traditional recipes,

00:01:53.023 --> 00:01:55.592
we're staying true to not only ourselves,

00:01:55.592 --> 00:01:58.791
but the region of the
food for which we serve,

00:01:58.791 --> 00:02:01.636
and we want to make
sure that you're leaving

00:02:01.636 --> 00:02:05.053
feeling like you got the true experience.

